    "result": "Excellent! The fix is confirmed working. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was in how the `frai` CLI passed arguments to the `frai-gate` subprocess. The action handler was relying on Commander.js's `args` parameter, which only captures positional arguments (like `init`) but not options (like `--ci`).\n\n**The fix:** Modified the gate command action handler (lines 737-755) to use `process.argv` to extract all arguments after the `gate` subcommand. This ensures both positional arguments and options are properly forwarded to the spawned `frai-gate` process.\n\nThe test confirms:\n- \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md` created\n- \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` created (this was missing before the fix)",
